Spirula Studio for Sparky Stereo OS
==================================

The package ships Vulkan by default and a separately installed CUDA build.
NVIDIA hardware setup configures the edition's signed CUDA repository and
its driver lock. The CUDA backend depends on NVIDIA's cudart package from
that repository; it never includes a private copy of the runtime or toolkit.

Model packages contain declarations and notices, never model weights.
Only the person can answer a required licence question. A missing profile
routes to its AppCenter package page. Purge removes installer-owned models;
ordinary removal keeps them. Other files in the model folder are retained.

Build tools: Debian's C/C++ toolchain, NVIDIA CUDA 13.5 (nvcc and cudart-dev),
and upstream Slang 2026.12.0.1. The recipe pins the Slang compiler archive's
address and SHA256 and downloads it only in the disposable build tree.
GLFW, Dear ImGui and CJK font source components have their original licences.
No model profile is downloaded while building the application.

Packaging-only icon revisions may use SPIRULA_REPACK_FROM pointing to the exact
qualified predecessor archive directory. The source carries every required hash.
The adapter rejects changed native source/components, changed runtime controls
and unrelated authored packaging inputs, restores original text through its HR
companion, and re-runs the payload and archive-backed link/start gates. It never
invokes a native compiler. Ordinary cold source builds remain the default.
